[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-18
TITLE: Grid control clock - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall generate a stable grid control clock within the frequency
range specified by the SRS and shall leave the grid-clock output inactive when
the clock is disabled.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A treatment plan should be ready to load.
* An oscilloscope or logic analyzer is connected to the grid-clock output.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Load a treatment plan.
3. Observe the grid-clock output with the measurement instrument.
4. Measure the grid-clock frequency.
5. Disable the grid clock using the approved service or test control.
6. Observe the grid-clock output after disabling it.
7. Re-enable the grid clock and observe the output.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
3. Verify the grid-clock output is present when enabled.
4. Verify the measured frequency is between 1 kHz and 20 kHz.
5. Verify the clock stops when disabled.
6. Verify the output remains inactive after disabling the clock.
7. Verify the clock restarts cleanly when re-enabled.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-19
TITLE: Elapsed-time high-voltage regulation - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that high-voltage closed-loop commands use elapsed-time ramp rates, bounded output, feedback
stability timing, and feedback-discrepancy cancellation.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on with high-voltage control unlocked and emission inactive.
* An HVPS test fixture can control high-voltage feedback independently of the requested setpoint.
* An approved diagnostic trace can capture requested voltage, feedback, DAC command,
  high-voltage-ramping status, and timestamps with at most 1 ms resolution.
* The default high-voltage configuration values are loaded.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Request increasing and decreasing high-voltage targets while using the fixture to produce
   absolute feedback errors below 5 kV, from 5 kV through less than 20 kV, and at least 20 kV.
2. Capture consecutive high-voltage commands and their timestamps in each error band.
3. Drive feedback through the requested target, then supply samples within +/-2% interspersed with
   samples outside that tolerance, and observe the high-voltage-ramping status immediately before
   and after 4000 ms of accumulated in-tolerance sample time.
4. Request values that exercise the lower and configured 100 kV upper command limits.
5. During an increasing ramp, hold feedback so the command is at least 50 kV and exceeds feedback by
   more than 50 kV.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the firmware evaluates the ramp on the 5 ms feedback-control cadence in both directions.
2. Verify the default command changes by 0.025 kV per cycle below 5 kV error and 0.1 kV per cycle in
   both larger error bands, corresponding to 5 kV/s and 20 kV/s elapsed-time rates.
3. Verify only samples within +/-2% add 5 ms to stability time, the ramping status remains set
   before the accumulator reaches 4000 ms, and the status clears on the first sample at or above
   that threshold.
4. Verify the command never falls below 0 kV or exceeds the configured 100 kV maximum.
5. Verify the feedback-discrepancy condition sets the command to zero and clears the ramping status.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-8
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-11
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-14
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-20
TITLE: Main control reporting - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered on, LED4 on mainboard should pulse at a rate much faster than
1 Hz.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* The silkscreen reference for LED4 is DS2206
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Check LED4 on the Main Board.
3. Measure the pulsing of the LED4 on the Main board.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify it's pulsing.
3. Verify it's pulsing at a rate much faster than 1 Hz.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-4
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-21
TITLE: HVPS digital status signals - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that the firmware reports HVPS digital signals, reports a distinct latched status for each
monitored fault source, and interprets the OC_CAT fault input as active-low both during startup and
during operation.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is connected to a test fixture capable of holding or toggling each HVPS fault input.
* The user of the system has service-user access.
* A treatment plan is ready to load.
* The service screen and an approved fault report or diagnostic trace are available.
* The approved clear-fault control is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Hold all HVPS fault inputs inactive and power on the system.
2. Open the service screen.
3. Record the reported HVPS digital status before emission.
4. Load a treatment plan and record the reported HVPS digital status during emission.
5. In turn, assert the FIL_CLK, CAT_ARC, FAN, OC_24, MASTER, OC_HV, TEMP_1, TEMP_3, and TEMP_2
   fault inputs, observe the report or diagnostic trace, and then deassert each input.
6. After each input is deasserted, record its reported fault status.
7. Use the approved clear-fault control and observe the fault status and diagnostic trace.
8. Confirm that OC_CAT is high, drive it from high to low, observe the report, and then return it
   high.
9. Record the cathode-overcurrent fault status after OC_CAT returns high.
10. Clear the reported fault.
11. Power off the system, hold OC_CAT low, and power on the system again.
12. Observe the fault report or diagnostic trace produced during startup.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system starts successfully with no fault status reported while the inputs are
   inactive.
2. Verify the service screen is displayed.
3. Verify the reported HVPS status indicates no high voltage before emission.
4. Verify the plan loads and the reported HVPS status indicates high voltage during emission.
5. Verify each asserted active-high source sets its own status bit and produces a diagnostic entry
   identifying that source and its status and input bit positions.
6. Verify each fault status remains latched after its input is deasserted.
7. Verify the explicit clear removes all latched fault flags and produces a diagnostic cleared entry
   for each cleared source.
8. Verify the high-to-low transition is interpreted as OC_CAT assertion and reports a distinct
   cathode-overcurrent fault.
9. Verify the cathode-overcurrent status remains latched after OC_CAT is deasserted.
10. Verify the cathode-overcurrent status clears.
11. Verify the low startup level is interpreted as OC_CAT assertion.
12. Verify a cathode-overcurrent fault is reported during initial input sampling.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-5
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-22
TITLE: Filament current setpoint - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered, the service user should check the reported value of filament current
in the Service screen with / without a running treatment plan.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* The user of the system needs to be a service user.
* A treatment plan should be ready to load.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Click Services symbol in the left side of the screen.
3. Look for value of filament current in the service screen.
4. Load a treatment plan.
5. Check the status of the system.
6. Look for value of filament current in the service screen.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the service screen displayed.
3. Record the value and verify the output control signal of the filament current is provided by firmware application.
4. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
5. Verify the status of the system is ready.
6. Record the value and verify the output control signal of the filament current is provided by firmware application.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-6
  ROLE: Verifies

