[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-35
TITLE: External ADC feedback acquisition - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that the firmware reads high-voltage and cathode-current feedback and reports
the correct values in UCSI.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and connected to UCSI with live telemetry available.
* A signal source or HVPS test fixture can provide known feedback inputs.
* Expected high-voltage and cathode-current values and acceptable measurement tolerances
  are defined for the selected inputs.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Apply known high-voltage and cathode-current feedback inputs.
2. Observe and record the corresponding feedback values in UCSI.
3. Change each input separately and verify the corresponding displayed value updates.
4. Repeat for low, middle, and high values within the approved operating range.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify both feedback values are available in UCSI.
2. Verify the displayed values match the expected values within the defined tolerances.
3. Verify changing either input updates the corresponding feedback value without incorrectly
   changing the other.
4. Verify the displayed values remain within the defined tolerances at all tested inputs.
<<<
